title every byte a file name may hold

# One fixture for the whole escaping rule. The names below carry an
# '=' (which would otherwise read as the content separator), a
# newline, a backslash, an edge space (which the trim would eat), a
# tab, and an invalid-UTF-8 byte -- none of which can appear
# literally in a line-oriented ASCII-only fixture.
#
# The encoding is mtree(5)'s: a backslash and exactly three octal
# digits. It is the same encoding the output manifest uses, which is
# the point -- a path decoded from a fixture and a path decoded from
# a manifest compare directly, with nothing in between.

tree base
  1-1: /
    2-100: eq\075uals = v1
    3-100: new\012line
    4-100: back\134slash
    5-100: edgespace\040
    6-100: tab\011sep
    7-100: bad\377utf8
